# {{.Name}}

This is a **Reliant Forge** project (github.com/reliant-labs/forge), driven by the `{{.CLI}}` CLI — not Atlassian Forge, Foundry's `forge` or Laravel Forge.
{{- if .Site}} It is a **static site**: a frontend with no backend, shipped by forge with environments, build-once releases{{if .ScaffoldEnvs}} and hosted static hosting{{end}}.{{end}}
{{- if .Container}} It is an **adopted app**: a server forge did not write, in any language, built from its own Dockerfile and shipped by forge with environments, build-once releases and Reliant hosting.
{{- else if .Adopted}} It is an **adopted project**: an existing app, in its own language and layout, that uses only the pieces of forge it opted into.{{end}}

This file holds the rules; depth is one `{{.CLI}} skill load <name>` away, named where you need it.

## Engineering disposition

A long-lived product: for anything hard to change later (architecture, public APIs, schemas), argue the alternatives against your own pick and choose the durable design, never a hack. Trivial work: just do it.

