## Use forge skills to guide your work

Load a skill before guessing, `{{.CLI}} skill load forge` first (what forge already scaffolds, so you never hand-write it); `{{.CLI}} skill list` is the catalog. `{{.CLI}} project shapes --grep <Name>` finds a symbol in every layer with file:line, `{{.CLI}} project capabilities` lists every verb, and `{{.CLI}} project libraries <pkg>` prints a forge library's API.

## Critical rules

1. **Never edit generated code** (`gen/`, `*_gen.go`, `*-hooks.ts`): edit its input (a proto, a migration, config, a `//forge:contract` type) and run `{{.CLI}} generate`. Handlers, `internal/app/providers.go` and `compose.go` are yours.
2. **Proto is the API's canonical input; migrations are the DB source of truth.** The ORM is projected from the applied `db/migrations` schema, never from proto.
3. **Iterate on what you changed; run the full gate ONCE, before you finish.** While iterating: `{{.CLI}} lint --scope <changed path>` (~10s; the full lint takes minutes) and {{if $taskGate}}`task test:short -- ./internal/<pkg>/...`{{else}}`go test -short ./internal/<pkg>/...`{{end}} (cached; never add `-count=1` or `-race`). To finish: `{{.CLI}} generate && {{.CLI}} lint && go build ./...{{if $taskGate}} && task test{{else}}{{range .Gate.Commands}}{{if eq .Does "tests"}} && {{.Run}}{{end}}{{end}}{{end}}`. Never pipe lint through `head`: the verdict is the LAST line (`--quiet` prints only failures).
{{- if not $taskGate}}
   **This project has no Taskfile, so there is no `task test` and no `{{.CLI}} test`.** {{template "gate-commands" .}}
{{- end}}
4. **A test over ~2s calls `testkit.Slow(t, "<why>")` first** (`github.com/reliant-labs/forge/pkg/testkit`): it skips under {{if $taskGate}}`test:short`, so a green `test:short` never ran it{{else}}`-short`, so a green `-short` run never ran it{{end}} (`testing`). Wait with `testkit.Eventually`/`testkit.Receive`, never `time.Sleep`. Run work over ~2 minutes in the background, never detached (`nohup`, `&`); `⏳ waiting for a heavy slot` is a queue: never kill its holders (`ci/slots`).
5. **Debugging: `{{.CLI}} skill load debug` first.** Frontend `console.*` calls and uncaught errors are on disk beside the backend logs: `grep '\[browser:error\]' .forge/logs/dev/*.log`.
6. **`auth_required: false` publishes one RPC, never a page.** Public pages are the route guard's `publicExactPaths`; access checks and row scoping are your handler code (`middleware.GetUser`), never generated (`auth`).

## Where logic goes

This is a Go project; `architecture` maps the tree. An rpc's logic is its `*Service` method in `internal/handlers/<svc>/rpc_<name>.go`, reaching collaborators through `s.deps` (`api`). Errors cross the rpc boundary as `return nil, svcerr.Wrap(err)` (`api`). Shared logic: `{{.CLI}} scaffold package <name>` (`service-layer`). Transactions: `s.deps.DB.RunTx(ctx, orm.Serializable, …)` (`service-layer/transactions`). Wiring: `internal/app/` (`services`). An rpc is CRUD only by its exact name, and list filters are `optional` (`proto`, `authoring`).
{{- if .Unmanaged}}

**Services forge does not manage:** {{range $i, $s := .Unmanaged}}{{if $i}}, {{end}}`{{$s}}`{{end}} (`// forge:unmanaged`).
Their handlers stay where this project already keeps them: buf still
generates their code, forge scaffolds nothing for them, and the layout above
does not apply to them. Never move one into `internal/handlers/` unless the
user asks; adopting a service means removing its marker, one service per PR
(`migration` skill). `{{.CLI}} project audit` lists them.
{{- end}}

## The scaffolded frontend is starter code

The dashboard, nav, sign-in screen and CRUD pages prove the stack is wired; rewriting them is expected (they are neutral on purpose). Load `frontend/design` before showing any of it to a user.

## Shipping

{{if .ScaffoldEnvs -}}
`{{.CLI}} env deploy <env>` ships to Reliant hosting (staging/prod are already bound to it), then `{{.CLI}} obs check <env> --wait --json` proves it (`deploy`).
{{- else -}}
`{{.CLI}} env deploy <env>` ships an env to wherever its `deploy/kcl/<env>/main.k` binds it, then `{{.CLI}} obs check <env> --wait --json` proves it (`deploy`). {{template "real-envs" .}}
{{- end}} Without hosting billing a backend deploy exits 7 and prints the billing link: give it to the user, don't retry (what is free: `deploy/hosted-capacity`). Never ask for `forge login` under Reliant; signed out, `--claimable` deploys and prints a claim link (`deploy/hosting`).

{{end -}}
## When forge itself is wrong — FIX IT

Bad codegen, a lint false positive, a scaffold quirk: fix it in forge when you can (semver at major 1: deprecate, never break), never by hand-editing generated output. Otherwise report it and carry on — forge's own defects only, not this project's code or tests. Never put credentials or file contents in a report:

    {{.CLI}} report-bug --severity high --title "<one line naming the defect>" \
      --actual "<the exact error text>" --evidence "<commands, output, file paths>"

