## What this project is

A static site — a landing page, marketing or docs site, SPA or PWA — is a complete forge project on its own, with **no backend**: no Go module, server, database or proto. `{{.CLI}} generate` skips every Go step by itself and there is no `go build`; never add a `go.mod`, `proto/` or `cmd/` to "make forge work". The site (`package.json`, `src/`, `public/`) is a plain Next.js or Vite app, and yours. forge owns `forge.yaml` and `deploy/kcl/<env>/main.k`, one per env ({{if .ScaffoldEnvs}}dev on its dev server; staging and prod on hosted static hosting{{else if .DeployEnvs}}{{range $i, $e := .DeployEnvs}}{{if $i}}, {{end}}{{$e}}{{end}}{{else}}none declared yet{{end}}), which declares the frontend's `type` and `public_dir`; check a change with `{{.CLI}} env render <env>`.

**Load `{{.CLI}} skill load deploy/static-site`** for the whole flow: envs, the static export, releases, hosting, runtime config, domains, adding an API. Also `frontend/design`, `deploy/domains`, `deploy/hosting`, `debug`.

## Run, build, ship

```bash
{{.CLI}} env up dev                          # the dev server; mirrors the browser console to .forge/logs/dev/
{{- if .ScaffoldEnvs}}
{{.CLI}} lint --static-export && {{.CLI}} env render prod
{{.CLI}} env build prod --release v0.1.0     # build ONCE, push, record the release
{{.CLI}} env deploy staging v0.1.0           # promote the same bytes …
{{.CLI}} env deploy prod v0.1.0              # … to prod, by digest — no rebuild
{{- else}}
{{.CLI}} lint --static-export && {{.CLI}} env render <env>
{{.CLI}} env build <env> --release v0.1.0    # build ONCE, push, record the release
{{.CLI}} env deploy <env> v0.1.0             # promote the same bytes to each env in turn, by digest
{{- end}}
```

Browser `console.*` calls, uncaught errors and unhandled rejections land in `.forge/logs/<env>/frontend_<name>.log` as `[browser:<level>]`: `grep '\[browser:error\]' .forge/logs/dev/*.log` before guessing.

`npm run build` must emit plain files (`out/` for Next.js `output: "export"`, `dist/` for Vite); `{{.CLI}} lint --static-export` names what a static export refuses, with file:line.
{{- if not .ScaffoldEnvs}} {{template "real-envs" .}}{{end}} A hosted deploy ships only a recorded release; recovery rolls forward. Build-time config is `env_vars` in each env's `main.k`; per-env config without a rebuild is `runtime_config` (`config.js`). Everything in a static site is public: never put a secret in either.

**Billing.** Free static hosting covers one organization per person (one they founded), with no limit on its sites; each env's site is one, within 1 GiB stored per site (`deploy/hosting`). A site in another organization, or any backend or database, needs hosting billing; until then `env deploy` exits 7 and prints the billing link. Give the user that link; don't retry. Never ask for `forge login` under Reliant.

**Custom domains{{if not .ScaffoldEnvs}} (on Reliant hosting){{end}}:** `{{.CLI}} domain add <host> --env {{$prod}}`.

