## Database migrations

{{if .Hook -}}
The schema migrations are {{.Tool}}'s, in `{{.Evidence}}`: forge.yaml `database.migrations` declares the tool, and forge runs it wherever it would apply its own migrations (`{{$.CLI}} db migrate up`, `status`). Keep writing migrations with {{.Tool}}.
{{- else if eq .Tool "forge" -}}
`{{.Evidence}}` holds forge migrations, applied by forge's migrator (`{{$.CLI}} db migrate up`). Load `db` before writing one.
{{- else if .Tool -}}
The schema migrations are {{.Tool}}'s (`{{.Evidence}}`){{with .Apply}}, applied with `{{.}}`{{end}}. They stay with {{.Tool}}.
{{- else -}}
`{{.Evidence}}` holds the app's migrations, and nothing says which tool applies them: ask the user before running any.
{{- end}}
{{- if ne .Tool "forge"}} Never convert them to forge migrations, rename or move them unless the user asks.{{end}}
{{- if $deploy}} On a forge-deployed env, run them before each rollout as a `kind = "job"` workload from the app's image with `before = [fw.BEFORE_ALL]` (`adopt/deploy` has the template).{{end}}
{{- end}}
